        "# Tribolium synteny: all-vs-all cross-check (v4)\n",
        "\n",
        "Four genomes, every pair compared **in the same way** (6 pairs): *T. castaneum* (`Tcas`), *T. madens* (`Tmad`), *T. freemani* (`Tfre`), *T. confusum* (`Tcon`).\n",
        "\n",
        "The *T. castaneum* reference is now **icTriCast1.1 (NCBI RefSeq GCF_031307605.1; annotation GCF_031307605.1-RS_2024_04)** rather than Tcas5.2.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What changed from v3**\n",
        "- Tcas input is the icTriCast1.1 genome FASTA and its matching NCBI GFF annotation.\n",
        "- Tcas linkage-group labels are read directly from the `region` records in the icTriCast1.1 GFF (`chromosome` attribute). The notebook no longer downloads or cross-tabulates the old Tcas5.2 GFF.\n",
        "- The old-assembly gene-ID crosswalk was removed. NCBI reports incomplete assembly-to-assembly remapping between Tcas5.2 and icTriCast1.1, so the old crosswalk should not be the default source of chromosome labels.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Before you run**\n",
        "1. Upload the eight files to `/content`: `Tcas_Anno.gff`, `Tcas_FASTA.fna`, `Tmad_Anno.gff3`, `Tmad_FASTA.fna`, `Tfree_Anno.gff`, `Tfree_FASTA.fna`, `Tcon_Anno.gff`, `Tcon_FASTA.fna`.\n",
        "2. For the two Tcas files, use the matching **GCF_031307605.1 / icTriCast1.1** downloads. Rename them to `Tcas_Anno.gff` and `Tcas_FASTA.fna` (or update `FILE_PREFIX` in the configuration cell if you prefer to keep their original names).\n",
        "3. Run the genome overview cell and check the Tcas sequence names and lengths. Confirm the chromosome labels are `LG1`–`LG10` and `LGX` as expected; the exact set depends on which primary/mitochondrial/unplaced sequences are present and the minimum-length filter.\n",
        "4. `Tmad` is scaffold-level, so check `MIN_LEN['Tmad']` before trusting anything for that species.\n",
        "5. Runtime is dominated by the 12 DIAMOND searches (several minutes each on a free Colab CPU).\n",
        "\n",
        "Any \"rearrangement\" between very close species is partly a measure of your false-positive rate. Read the supported (tier A/B) breakpoints, not the raw count.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Important:** all Tcas coordinates and sequence IDs in the outputs will now refer to icTriCast1.1, not Tcas5.2. Do not mix old Tcas5.2 coordinates or BAM files with this run."
      ]
    },
