        "## 7. Triangulation in icTriCast1.1 Tcas coordinates\n",
        "Breakpoints from icTriCast1.1 Tcas-vs-Tmad, Tcas-vs-Tfre and Tcas-vs-Tcon are all in Tcas coordinates, so they can be matched. Events within `TRI_PAD` on the same Tcas sequence are treated as one locus. For each locus the table shows the best tier in each comparison (A / B / C = unresolved / `-` = not found).\n",
        "\n",
        "Reading it (assuming Tcas is not itself the odd one out): a locus found against **only one** species suggests that species differs from the others; a locus found against **all three** suggests the difference is in Tcas (or ancestral-vs-derived state differs in Tcas). Tier C entries are not evidence either way. This is a screening table, not a phylogenetic inference."
      ]
    },
